WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congrats on the film.
-Thanks very much.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.303
-This is about Molly Bloom.
This is a true life story.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.571 line:92%
-It's an absolutely true story.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
Molly Bloom,
in her 20s and 30s,

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:09.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
ran the world's most exclusive
high-stakes poker game.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Movie stars, sports stars,
politicians,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.281 size:81% position:41%
hedge-fund managers,
they would win or lose

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
millions of dollars
in the course of a night,

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes in the course
of a hand.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:24.324
And it was all legal until
she crossed a very thin line.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:26.159 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And even then, nobody --

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:30.296 size:78% position:39%
She wasn't in trouble
until she unknowingly

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.832 size:75% position:38%
invited four members
of the Russian Mafia

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play in the game.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's when the FBI
got interested.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is a --
That is a problem.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
In general,
they say the limit

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
is three Russian mob guys
at any --

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.809
-Yeah, and she invited four.
-The fourth one's the killer.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:46.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And also, unknowingly,
an FBI informant.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, that's not very good.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the thing is, she was --
one of her --

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
her expertise
was vetting players,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
was knowing exactly
who was sitting at her table.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
So even though she was facing
five years in jail,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
she was mostly
really embarrassed.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Oh, well.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:07.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
This -- This movie has classic
Aaron Sorkin dialogue,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.469
which I'm a great fan of,
but this is the first time

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:12.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
you directed
and you ended up directing

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
a script
written by Aaron Sorkin.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Did you realize now

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
the difficulty
that directors maybe have had

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the years
directing your scripts?

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't under--
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.650 size:81% position:41%
Don't understand why
at least three of them

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.820
haven't punched me in the face.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
I called --
On the second day of shooting,

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
I called David Fincher, who
directed "The Social Network."

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:36.396
And I said, "David, where do you
have the actors breathe

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.164 line:92%
when they're doing my stuff?"

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.167
and this is the sound he made --
[ Chuckles mischievously ]

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You actually had
an Oscar-winning director

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
on your film,
which is Kevin Costner.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.910
-Yes.
Kevin was incredibly supportive,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.778 size:84% position:42% line:92%
incredibly encouraging.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
He would remind me
from time to time that

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.417
when he directed his first film,
"Dances With Wolves,"

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
he had to worry about
which direction

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
5,000 buffalo were gonna run
when he called action.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.190
-Yeah.
-And were they gonna come back.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I talked
to a number of directors,

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
including a friend of yours,
Adam McKay.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
"The Big Short."

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Big Short."
Who was very encouraging.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody --
I didn't write this movie

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.205 line:92%
thinking I was gonna direct it.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:19.939 size:84% position:42% line:92%
When I write something,

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want the very best director
to direct it.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's never me.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I wrote it
and delivered the first draft,

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.183
and the producers encouraged me
to direct it.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the thing is --
This is for real.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.589
After describing all the glamour
and the decadence and the money

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.926
and the poker and everything,
the movie does have all of that,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.895 size:78% position:39%
but it's set against
the backdrop of that.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's actually --
and this isn't a joke --

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a Christmas movie.
-Really?

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is a very -- Molly Bloom
is a very inspirational,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:50.870 size:84% position:42% line:92%
aspirational character.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.606
And, ultimately, it's a story
about doing the right thing

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:57.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the wrong thing is
a lot easier, more profitable,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.378 line:92%
can keep you out of jail.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:04.517 size:81% position:41%
Basically, she refused
to dish on the players

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.351 line:92%
who were playing in the game,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is what the Justice
Department wanted her to do.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The other amazing thing
about her story,

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is taken care of
in the film,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that she was
an Olympic skier.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, obviously, there are many
poker scenes in the film.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Directing that requires
a level of skill,

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I imagine
the technical expertise

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.368 line:92%
required to shoot a skiing scene

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
is more intimidating
as a first-time director.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:28.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were -- Yes.
Molly Bloom came --

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was ranked third
in North America

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in women's moguls.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a form
of skiing which is

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
tch tch tch tch tch,
fwt fwt fwt, psh psh psh!

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just -- It looks like
a terrible way to die.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.220 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was ranked third
in North America.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:46.693
Came about 100 yards from making
the U.S. Olympic ski team,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
when --
This isn't a spoiler.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
It happens in
the first eight minutes.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
When she literally
and metaphorically

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
trips over a stick

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.272 line:92%
and literally and metaphorically

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
flies way off course
in her life.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:07.247
Directing those scenes, we were
on an actual World Cup slope,

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.948 size:75% position:38% line:92%
which is 52 degrees.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.883 line:92%
It's slanted about like that.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I have to tell you,
honestly,

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a problem
on a flat surface that's dry.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:16.956 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fall down
for no reason at all.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:22.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm standing
on this 52-degree ice wall,

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:28.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to confidently
give instructions to the crew,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.302 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to the stunt skiers,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.504 size:84% position:42%
to people who were used
to this kind of thing.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.840 size:81% position:41%
And I would start out,
"All right, on action,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna --" Fwt!
and I would just fall down,

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:38.144 line:92%
and somebody would lift me up.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay, sorry.
Guys, on action,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna cut --
Damn it!

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it would
take me 10 minutes

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.586
to get a direction out
'cause I just couldn't stand up.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, finally,
just two guys on the crew

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
just held me up under each arm
while I directed the movie.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was humiliating.
-I think, you know, it's --

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:57.130
When you think of Molly Bloom
and this incredible story,

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:57.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it almost seems sad

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.466 size:84% position:42%
that a man who couldn't
even stand in snow --

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.135 size:75% position:38%
-No, I couldn't even
stand in the snow.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.471
And, by the way, also, can't --
I can't play poker.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.205 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm not a poker player.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.207 size:78% position:39%
But all of the extras
in the poker scenes

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.610
were professional poker players.
I wanted it that way.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.479
Professional poker players
have a way of handling cards

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.349
and chips that's just different
from me and you.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:20.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, extras are paid
about $90 for a 12-hour day.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're not paid
very much at all.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they didn't care,
because every big-shot actor

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:28.828
that came in, like Michael Cera
and Chris O'Dowd,

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
would come in
and do their poker scenes.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.366
Any time we were changing
lenses, changing lighting,

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.736
moving the cameras, the dealer,
who was a professional dealer,

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:37.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
would just start
to deal a round.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
The actors would always
want to play with the pros.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.909 size:75% position:38%
The actors went home
without their pants.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:43.443 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:46.446
And the extras were the
highest-paid actors on the set.

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:49.482
-Well, there's something fitting
about that, as well.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:50.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really a wonderful film.
-Thanks very much.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.985
-Congratulations
on the Golden Globe nomination.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I appreciate it.
Christmas Day!

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Christmas Day!
Aaron Sorkin, everybody!

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:01.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Molly's Game," Christmas Day,
nationwide on January 5th!

